From 1d54014989a583732724d87f1c9cf6e5e77d7c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Freddie Jheng <Freddie.Jheng@quantatw.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:59:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add support for MTIA CPERs

MTIA (Meta Training and Inference Accelerator) devices report errors
to the BMC as CPER records with an OEM section (GUID
c8f67ddf-e784-471d-a05f-7c70a7a11ad6). Add a parser, generator, JSON
schema and example for this section.

The section is a fixed 120-byte record, published as a single "mtia"
JSON object:
- version and recordSize of the record.
- pcieDeviceId: the PCIe identity of the reporting device, decoded into
  vendor ID, device ID and the function, device, bus, segment and slot
  numbers. Published only when validation bit 0 is set.
- deviceSerial: the device serial number. Published only when
  validation bit 1 is set.
- bootTimer: the event time since boot, in nanoseconds.
- eventId and severity of the event.
- scope, chipId, platformId, skuId, chipletId and moduleId: identify
  where the event was generated, published as hex strings.
- detailFormatId: the format of the event detail payload, published as
  a hex string.
- eventDetailRaw: the event detail payload, published as-is in base64.
  Only the first detailLength bytes are published. detailLength itself
  is not published, since it is implied by the payload length.

Change-Id: Ib41661a9944796b2c26664a6172a3a9a5bc4039a
Signed-off-by: Freddie Jheng <Freddie.Jheng@quantatw.com>
